  "findings": [
    "The most-read theme does not bring buyers: Filling the calendar had 5,367 sessions and 26 key events (0.48 per 100 sessions against 2.01 for all content), and its seed demand (4,370 a month) is under the median (4,460). It is dropped: no new pieces, existing ones stay up.",
    "Choosing booking software converts best: 3.86 key events per 100 sessions on 985 sessions, so the gap pieces use it.",
    "Content for comparing and deciding is almost all for salons: 3 gaps (Clinic practice managers at Compare, Clinic practice managers at Decide, Fitness studios and trainers at Compare) and 1 thin cell (Fitness studios and trainers at Decide). They are filled in weeks 1 to 6 and 7 to 13.",
    "Newsletters went out 18 times in 12 months with 3 empty months, so the plan holds 4 a quarter. The 8 help articles came in one push (6 in one month), so that month is left out and their pace is 1 a quarter, not 2.",
    "Client intake forms has no pieces but the highest seed demand (6,880 a month) and comes straight from the clinics' buying question, so it is a Build theme with 2 test articles."
  ],
